    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2FEnkbKDW2SF6o1VMULYvEt)_\n\nNew module `sp-litnotes-meta` (doc: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-litnotes-meta.org`). After `citar-create-note` it fills the first section of the note from the BibTeX entry:\n\n- `pub-author`: one link per author (`author`, else `editor`). Matched by name against existing notes in the Vulpea db (a `person` note wins); if none exists, a new `person` note with an ID is written and linked.\n- `pub-title`, `pub-year` (year, else `date`, else the crossref's year).\n- `bib-parent`: link to the litnote of the `crossref`d entry, only if that note exists (otherwise left out, with a message).\n- `bib-project`: minibuffer picker over notes tagged `project`, default the thesis.\n\nExisting values are never changed. `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill` does the same for an existing note; `sp-litnotes-meta-auto` turns the advice off.\n\nTests: `tests/sp-litnotes-meta-test.el` (6 pass in Emacs 29, Vulpea stubbed). Not run on the real vault or with real `citar-vulpea`: the note file must exist on disk right after `citar-create-note` for the advice to find it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAax2Ln1zC1FyubuGs)_",
